  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Hypersexualization",
  "description": "The meme uses the phrase 'farm equipment and livestock don't mix' to imply that the Black man is 'livestock' and the white woman is 'farm equipment,' which is a form of hypersexualization. This stereotype dehumanizes Black men by portraying them as objects for the use or control of white women, reducing their humanity and dignity. This is a well-documented racist trope in American culture.",
